    {
      "id": "ARCH-006",
      "decision": "Brutalist Monotone UI Refactor",
      "rationale": "A black-on-white monotone theme with brutalist aesthetics provides a high-contrast, focused experience, while allowing highlights for critical feedback.",
      "affects": [
        "frontend/style.css",
        "frontend/components"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ARCH-007",
      "decision": "Router-driven auth with a single reactive auth store; App.vue stops branching on localStorage.",
      "rationale": "Today App.vue reads localStorage in parallel to vue-router and re-syncs via watch(route.path). This breaks deep links (refresh on /student lands on the right component but the nav re-flickers and any consumer of isLoggedIn/user that mounts before the watch fires sees stale data), and a stale user object can persist after token expiry because nothing invalidates it. A single source of truth \u2014 vue-router for *where* the user is, and a reactive auth store for *who* they are \u2014 eliminates the dual state machine, makes 401 handling possible in one place, and lets meta-driven guards do the role checking instead of v-if soup in App.vue.",
      "affects": [
        "frontend/src/router.ts",
        "frontend/src/App.vue",
        "frontend/src/main.ts",
        "frontend/src/services/auth.ts",
        "frontend/src/components/LoginView.vue"
      ],
      "design_notes": "CREATE `frontend/src/services/auth.ts` exporting a module-level reactive store and a `useAuth()` composable. Public API:\n  - `interface AuthUser { id?: number; username: string; role: 'ADMIN'|'LECTURER'|'STUDENT' }`\n  - `const authState = reactive({ token: string|null, user: AuthUser|null })`  // module singleton\n  - `function useAuth()` returns `{ token, user, isLoggedIn (computed), login(token, user), logout(), hydrateFromStorage() }`\n  - `login(token, user)` writes both to localStorage (keys MUST remain `sql_quiz_token` and `sql_quiz_user` to avoid breaking existing storage) AND sets reactive state.\n  - `logout()` clears both storage keys and reactive state, then the caller (or a one-shot effect) navigates to `/login`.\n  - `hydrateFromStorage()` is called once from `main.ts` BEFORE `app.mount(...)` to seed state from localStorage. This guarantees no flicker on refresh.\n\nROUTER CHANGES (`frontend/src/router.ts`):\n  - Replace `meta.public` and `meta.role` (singular) with `meta.requiresAuth: boolean` (default true) and `meta.allowedRoles?: Role[]` (omit = any authenticated role).\n  - Per-route meta:\n    * `/login`           \u2192 `{ requiresAuth: false }`\n    * `/student`         \u2192 `{ requiresAuth: true, allowedRoles: ['STUDENT'] }`\n    * `/lecturer`        \u2192 `{ requiresAuth: true, allowedRoles: ['ADMIN','LECTURER'] }`\n    * `/admin`           \u2192 `{ requiresAuth: true, allowedRoles: ['ADMIN'] }`  (note: today's router lets ADMIN reach any meta.role, preserve this by listing ADMIN explicitly on lecturer-shared routes)\n    * `/practice`        \u2192 `{ requiresAuth: true, allowedRoles: ['STUDENT'] }`\n    * `/student/results` \u2192 `{ requiresAuth: true, allowedRoles: ['STUDENT'] }`\n    * `/lecturer/practice` \u2192 `{ requiresAuth: true, allowedRoles: ['ADMIN','LECTURER'] }`\n  - The existing `/dashboard` route currently uses `component: () => import('./App.vue')` which is wrong (it would mount App inside itself). Keep ONLY the `beforeEnter` redirect logic but switch the component to a tiny `RoleRedirect.vue` (or a `redirect: (to) => ...` function form) that reads `useAuth().user.value` instead of localStorage. Preferred: change `/dashboard` to `{ path: '/dashboard', redirect: () => { const u = useAuth().user.value; return u?.role === 'ADMIN' ? '/admin' : u?.role === 'LECTURER' ? '/lecturer' : u?.role === 'STUDENT' ? '/student' : '/login' } }`. Drop the `component` line.\n  - Single `router.beforeEach((to)) => { ... }` guard:\n    1. If `!to.meta.requiresAuth` (i.e. login) AND `useAuth().isLoggedIn.value` \u2192 redirect to `/dashboard` (so a logged-in user typing /login bounces to their home). EXCEPTION: if `to.query.force === '1'` allow through (for token expiry redirects).\n    2. If `to.meta.requiresAuth` AND `!isLoggedIn.value` \u2192 `next({ path: '/login', query: { redirect: to.fullPath } })`.\n    3. If `to.meta.allowedRoles` AND user.role NOT IN that list \u2192 `next({ name: 'forbidden' })` (see route below) OR fall back to `/dashboard` if `forbidden` isn't desired; choose `forbidden` so the user gets a clear message rather than a silent bounce.\n    4. Else `next()`.\n  - Add a `/403` route `{ path: '/403', name: 'forbidden', component: ForbiddenView, meta: { requiresAuth: false } }`. Keep ForbiddenView minimal (brutalist card, 'Forbidden', 'Return to your home' link that uses `useAuth().user.value?.role` to compute the target).\n\nAPP.VUE CHANGES:\n  - Delete `isLoggedIn`, `user`, `checkAuth`, the `onMounted`, and the `watch(route.path)`.\n  - Replace with `const { user, isLoggedIn, logout: doLogout } = useAuth()`.\n  - Template `v-if=\"isLoggedIn && user\"` becomes `v-if=\"isLoggedIn\"` (user is non-null whenever logged in).\n  - `logout` button handler: `await doLogout(); router.push('/login')`.\n  - `<main class=\"content\"><router-view /></main>` stays; no branching beyond that.\n\nLOGIN VIEW CHANGES (`LoginView.vue`):\n  - After successful POST, call `useAuth().login(data.token, data.user)` INSTEAD of writing localStorage directly. (login() owns the write.)\n  - Then `router.push((route.query.redirect as string) || '/dashboard')` so deep-link round-tripping works.\n\nMAIN.TS CHANGES:\n  - `import { useAuth } from './services/auth'; useAuth().hydrateFromStorage();` BEFORE `app.use(router); app.mount('#app')`.\n\nEDGE CASES (must be handled, tests will check these):\n  - Already-logged-in user hits `/login` directly \u2192 bounced to `/dashboard` (which redirects to their role home). Exception: if `?force=1` they reach login (used by expired-token redirect path).\n  - Deep link without auth: `/student/results` typed cold \u2192 guard sends to `/login?redirect=/student/results`; after login, LoginView pushes back to redirect target.\n  - Role mismatch: STUDENT typing `/admin` \u2192 redirected to `/403`, which offers a link to their role home.\n  - Token expiry: out of scope for this round (P1 \u2014 note in backlog); however, the auth store SHOULD be the only writer of localStorage so a future interceptor can call `useAuth().logout()` from one place.\n  - Hard refresh on a protected route while logged in: `hydrateFromStorage()` runs before mount, so `isLoggedIn` is true synchronously when the guard first runs \u2014 no flash of /login.\n\nDO NOT introduce Pinia for this round. A module-scoped `reactive()` is sufficient; revisit if state grows.\n\nCLARIFICATION (feedback-loop 2026-05-22): Error routes (not-found, forbidden) are exempt from Rule 1's auto-redirect so that logged-in users still see error pages. Rule 1's exception list must include the route names 'not-found' and 'forbidden' alongside the existing ?force=1 escape hatch; otherwise role-mismatched users redirected to /403 by Rule 3 are immediately bounced to /dashboard, and any logged-in user hitting an unknown URL is bounced away from the 404 page."
    },
    {
      "id": "ARCH-008",
      "decision": "Extract a reusable StudentMultiSelect.vue component (searchable, keyboard-navigable, with Select All / Select None), in-repo, replacing the inline checkbox list in LecturerView.vue.",
      "rationale": "Correction to the brief: LecturerView.vue does NOT use a comma-separated text input \u2014 it already has an inline checkbox list bound to `selectedStudentIds` (lines 675\u2013682) backed by `GET /api/v1/users/students`. The real gap is that the inline list has no search, no keyboard navigation, no select-all/none, no result count summary, and isn't reusable for future use cases (e.g. assigning students to practice sets, group emails). Building a small in-repo component preserves the brutalist monotone aesthetic exactly (a library would drag in styles that fight var(--color-border) and the sharp 2px borders) and avoids adding a runtime dependency for a contained UI concern. Backend endpoint is verified: `GET /api/v1/users/students` (NOT `/users?role=STUDENT` \u2014 the brief had that wrong; do not change the backend).",
      "affects": [
        "frontend/src/components/StudentMultiSelect.vue",
        "frontend/src/components/LecturerView.vue"
      ],
      "design_notes": "CREATE `frontend/src/components/StudentMultiSelect.vue` as a controlled component.\n\nPROPS (TypeScript):\n  - `modelValue: number[]`                    // selected student IDs (v-model)\n  - `students: Array<{ id: number; username: string }>`  // caller passes the list; this component does NOT fetch (keeps it pure, lets parent control loading state)\n  - `loading?: boolean`                       // optional, shows a 'Loading students...' state\n  - `placeholder?: string`                    // search input placeholder, default 'Search students...'\n  - `maxHeight?: string`                      // CSS, default '250px' to match current multi-select-box\n\nEMITS:\n  - `update:modelValue` (number[])\n\nBEHAVIOR:\n  - Internal `searchQuery` ref; filtered list is `students.filter(s => s.username.toLowerCase().includes(searchQuery.toLowerCase()))`. Case-insensitive substring match; do not implement fuzzy matching in this round.\n  - Header row inside the box: search input on the left; `[Select All]` and `[Select None]` text-buttons on the right. 'Select All' operates on the CURRENTLY FILTERED set (intuitive: if a user searches 'sec01', clicking Select All selects only the visible matches and merges with existing selection \u2014 do a union, not a replace). 'Select None' clears the FILTERED subset from the selection only (so unrelated selections elsewhere are preserved).\n  - Counter line below header: `'{n} of {total} selected'` where total = `students.length`.\n  - Each row: checkbox + label. The label is clickable (existing pattern).\n  - Keyboard navigation: arrow Up/Down moves a visual focus across rendered (filtered) rows; Space toggles the focused row; Enter does the same as Space; the search input has tabindex 0 and is the natural first focus stop; rows have tabindex -1 and use `@keydown` handlers on a wrapping div with `role=\"listbox\"`. Roving tabindex pattern: a single `focusedIndex` ref drives `:tabindex` per row.\n  - When the filtered list changes, clamp `focusedIndex` to a valid index (or -1 if empty).\n  - Empty state: 'No students match.' when filtered list is empty but `students.length > 0`; 'No students found.' when `students.length === 0` (preserves current wording).\n  - Styling: reuse `.multi-select-box`, `.student-item` look (2px black border, monospace font, sharp corners). Add a `.msel-toolbar` flex row at the top. No new colors.\n\nINTEGRATION IN LecturerView.vue (Assignments tab):\n  - Replace the inline `<div class=\"multi-select-box\">...</div>` block (lines ~674\u2013682) with `<StudentMultiSelect v-model=\"selectedStudentIds\" :students=\"studentsList\" />`.\n  - Keep `fetchStudents()` and the `studentsList` ref on LecturerView \u2014 the component remains presentation-only.\n  - The existing label `'Select Students ({{ selectedStudentIds.length }} selected):'` can be simplified or removed since the component shows its own counter; keep the outer `<label>` for the section heading but drop the count (avoid double-counting).\n  - Import path: `import StudentMultiSelect from './StudentMultiSelect.vue'`.\n\nACCESSIBILITY:\n  - Root `<div role=\"group\" aria-label=\"Student selector\">`.\n  - Search input has visible label OR `aria-label=\"Search students\"`.\n  - List uses `role=\"listbox\"` with `aria-multiselectable=\"true\"`; each row `role=\"option\"` with `aria-selected` reflecting checkbox state.\n\nOUT OF SCOPE FOR THIS ROUND:\n  - Virtual scrolling. Current rosters are small (<500). Note in backlog if it becomes an issue.\n  - Server-side search.\n  - Async chunked load."
    },
    {
      "id": "ARCH-009",
      "decision": "Add a catch-all 404 route and NotFoundView.vue with a role-aware 'Back to home' link.",
      "rationale": "Today the router has no catch-all; an unknown path lands on a blank `<router-view />` inside App.vue with the nav still rendered \u2014 confusing because nothing tells the user the path is bad. A typed 404 route lets the brutalist UI explicitly tell users where they are, and the role-aware home link plays well with ARCH-007's auth store. Keeping it as a separate view (not an inline template in App.vue) keeps App.vue dumb and aligns with the 'App renders router-view, nothing else' rule from ARCH-007.",
      "affects": [
        "frontend/src/components/NotFoundView.vue",
        "frontend/src/router.ts"
      ],
      "design_notes": "CREATE `frontend/src/components/NotFoundView.vue`:\n  - Brutalist card: thick 2px black border, white background, monospace mark `404` styled like the `.logo-mark` (border + mono).\n  - Heading: 'Page not found'.\n  - Body: 'The path \"{{ route.fullPath }}\" does not exist.' (use `useRoute()` to show the attempted path verbatim \u2014 helps debugging).\n  - Primary link: text 'Back to home' that resolves the target via `useAuth()`:\n    * if not logged in \u2192 `/login`\n    * STUDENT \u2192 `/student`\n    * LECTURER or ADMIN \u2192 `/lecturer`\n    Use `<router-link>` not raw `<a>`.\n  - Optional secondary action: 'Go back' that calls `router.back()` (only if `window.history.length > 1`).\n  - Reuse the `.card`, `.btn-primary` styles already established; do not invent new classes beyond a small `.notfound-shell` wrapper centering the card vertically/horizontally similar to `.login-shell`.\n\nROUTE REGISTRATION (`router.ts`):\n  - Append AT THE END of the routes array:\n    `{ path: '/:pathMatch(.*)*', name: 'not-found', component: () => import('./components/NotFoundView.vue'), meta: { requiresAuth: false } }`\n  - `meta.requiresAuth: false` is important: an unauthenticated user typing a junk URL should see 404, not be punted to /login (otherwise the user can't tell whether the URL was bad or auth was bad).\n  - Order matters in vue-router 4 only for ambiguous matches; since `/:pathMatch(.*)*` is the most permissive, it must be LAST.\n\nEDGE CASES:\n  - Typing `/admin` while logged in as STUDENT routes through the guard's role check \u2192 `/403`, NOT 404. Confirm by ordering: guard checks `requiresAuth` and `allowedRoles` first for matched routes; only truly unmatched paths fall to the catch-all.\n  - Logout while on `/not-found` (e.g. a stale tab): user stays on the page since `meta.requiresAuth: false`. The 'Back to home' link will resolve to `/login` because `isLoggedIn` is now false."
    },
    {
      "id": "ARCH-010",
      "decision": "Mobile responsiveness pass for <768px: stacked nav, fluid content, horizontal-scroll tables (one consistent strategy), media queries on App.vue and the four heavy views.",
      "rationale": "Viewport meta is already present (verified in index.html). Layouts break below 768px primarily because (a) `.nav-links` is a single flex row with 5\u20137 buttons that overflows, (b) `.content` has a fixed `max-width: 1200px` but no horizontal padding adjustment, (c) LecturerView's `form-grid` is `1fr 1fr` and squashes inputs, (d) `ResultTable` and `.preview-table` overflow without affordance on some viewports. We pick ONE table strategy \u2014 horizontal scroll with a subtle scroll affordance \u2014 because it preserves all columns (important for the consolidated scores table which has dynamic exam columns) and a card layout would require duplicating semantic content per row. The brutalist aesthetic favors a stacked nav (no hamburger / no JS toggle) which collapses into a vertical column under the logo at the breakpoint.",
      "affects": [
        "frontend/src/App.vue",
        "frontend/src/components/LecturerView.vue",
        "frontend/src/components/StudentView.vue",
        "frontend/src/components/ResultTable.vue",
        "frontend/src/style.css"
      ],
      "design_notes": "BREAKPOINT: single breakpoint `@media (max-width: 767.98px)`. Use 767.98 (not 768) to avoid double-matching at exactly 768.\n\nAPP.VUE (top nav):\n  - Below breakpoint: `.top-nav` becomes `flex-direction: column; align-items: stretch; padding: 0.6rem 1rem; gap: 0.6rem;`.\n  - `.nav-links` becomes `flex-direction: column; align-items: stretch; gap: 0.3rem;` and each button becomes full-width with `text-align: left`.\n  - `.user-info` becomes its own line `margin-right: 0; padding-bottom: 0.4rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border);`.\n  - `.logo` stays at the top.\n  - `.content` becomes `margin: 1.5rem auto; padding: 0 0.75rem; max-width: 100%;`. (Keep the 1200px cap above the breakpoint.)\n  - DO NOT introduce a hamburger or any JS-driven menu. Stacked is the spec.\n\nSTYLE.CSS (global utilities):\n  - Add a single `.responsive-table-wrap` class (matching `.preview-table-wrap`) with `overflow-x: auto; -webkit-overflow-scrolling: touch; border: 2px solid var(--color-border);` and a `::after` pseudo or right-side gradient hint to indicate scrollability when content overflows. Keep the affordance subtle (brutalist): a 12px wide right-edge linear-gradient from transparent to `rgba(0,0,0,0.08)` only when scrollable. If implementing the gradient is non-trivial without JS, fall back to a visible `\u2192` chevron hint inside the wrapper for mobile (CSS-only via `@media`).\n  - `.preview-table` (and any other table): below breakpoint, reduce `padding: 0.4rem 0.6rem` and `font-size: 0.8rem` to fit more on small screens before scroll kicks in.\n  - Add a utility `@media (max-width: 767.98px) { .form-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr !important; } }` so any caller using `.form-grid` becomes single-column. (LecturerView's `.full-width` already spans, which becomes a no-op when there is only 1 column \u2014 fine.)\n\nLECTURERVIEW.VUE:\n  - `.tab-bar` below breakpoint: change `flex: 1` to allow horizontal scroll. Set `.tab-bar { overflow-x: auto; flex-wrap: nowrap; }` and `.tab-bar button { flex: 0 0 auto; min-width: 110px; }`. Avoid stacking tabs vertically \u2014 keeps the brutalist horizontal rhythm.\n  - `.context-selector` becomes `flex-direction: column; align-items: stretch;` below breakpoint.\n  - `.exam-context-status` becomes `flex-direction: column; align-items: flex-start; gap: 0.5rem;` below breakpoint.\n  - The consolidated scores table is already wrapped in `.preview-table-wrap` (horizontal scroll). Verify and keep.\n  - The Results tab's header `<div style=\"display: flex; justify-content: space-between;\">` with the Export button must stack on mobile: extract that inline style into a scoped class `.results-header` and add a media-query rule to switch to `flex-direction: column; align-items: stretch;`.\n\nSTUDENTVIEW.VUE:\n  - Implementor should AUDIT for: fixed widths, inline styles enforcing horizontal layout, table without `.preview-table-wrap`. Apply `.responsive-table-wrap` (or existing `.preview-table-wrap`) to any bare table. Reduce `padding` and stack any `.form-grid` (already handled globally if class is used).\n\nRESULTTABLE.VUE:\n  - Ensure the outer container uses `.preview-table-wrap` (or new `.responsive-table-wrap`) so horizontal scroll kicks in. Do NOT convert rows to cards on mobile \u2014 column dimensionality matters here.\n  - If headers wrap awkwardly on mobile, set `white-space: nowrap` on `th` so a column either fits or contributes to overflow (the scroll affordance covers the rest).\n\nNOT IN SCOPE THIS ROUND (P1/P2 \u2014 document in `docs/ui_ux_backlog.md` per agent_notes):\n  - Card-per-row table layouts for any view.\n  - Hamburger / slide-in nav.\n  - Tablet breakpoint (768\u20131023). Acceptable for now to use desktop layout from 768 upward.\n  - Touch-target audit (44px minimum) beyond what naturally falls out of padding bumps.\n\nACCEPTANCE / SPOT-CHECK CRITERIA (validator):\n  - At 360px wide (iPhone SE), `.top-nav` does not horizontally scroll; all buttons are stacked and reachable.\n  - At 360px wide, the consolidated scores table scrolls horizontally without clipping content under the nav.\n  - At 768px exactly, desktop layout applies (single-line nav, two-column form-grid).\n  - No use of `position: fixed` for the nav (keeps brutalist + avoids viewport edge cases on iOS Safari)."
    }
  ],
  "todos": [],
  "in_progress": [],
