      "failure_source": "merge-check (step [5]) FAIL on frontend/src/router.ts",
      "failure_summary": "beforeEach Rule 1 (`!requiresAuth && isLoggedIn -> /dashboard`) unconditionally swallows /403 and the /:pathMatch(.*)* catch-all, because both routes carry meta.requiresAuth:false per ARCH-007 / ARCH-009. Consequence: ForbiddenView is unreachable for any logged-in user (role-mismatch flow /admin -> Rule3 name:forbidden -> Rule1 -> /dashboard -> role-home), and NotFoundView is unreachable for logged-in users hitting bad URLs. Affected TODOs: TODO-020 (router rework), TODO-021 (ForbiddenView), TODO-027 (catch-all).",
      "decision_rationale": "Option 1 (named-route exception in Rule 1) chosen. Option 2 (flip meta.requiresAuth to true on /403 and /404) regresses UX for unauthenticated users hitting bookmarked broken links by bouncing them to /login instead of showing the error page. Option 3 (different redirect target) is more invasive and not clearly better. Option 1 preserves the original ARCH-007 intent ('unauthenticated users can see error pages') with the smallest code change, keeps meta semantics intact, and parallels the existing ?force=1 escape hatch idiom.",
